2026-10-15 18:44 UTC — reconciled the `MessageClientExt` constructor surface.

The pinned Java source at `efa1be59d6fc747ad220f036c86030f05f0419f9` declares
no constructor on `MessageClientExt`; its public implicit constructor is
no-argument. The invoked Java fixture now reflects one public no-argument
constructor. Rust `MessageClientExt::new()` and `Default` match that
construction path; removed the public `new(MessageExt)` method and
`From<MessageExt>` implementation. Rustdoc compile-fail examples guard both
conversion surfaces. The decoder differential continues checking the
client-visible and physical IDs directly on decoded messages.

