2026-10-15 18:53 UTC — completed a re-export-aware Common inherent-method
crosswalk slice.

Generated the all-feature Common Rustdoc JSON with
`rustup run nightly cargo rustdoc --locked -p rocketmq-classic-common
--all-features -- -Z unstable-options --output-format json`. Traversing the
public re-export graph reached 26 aggregate types. Exact method-name search
initially found 13 names absent from compatibility tables. Source/test review
confirmed the Java mappings and added explicit rows for mutable `getBody`
contents, nullable `hasProperty` and `putUserProperty`, `MessageHostAddress`
to `InetSocketAddress` adapters, `MessageId` setters, and the public
`TopicValidator` set getters. The final name sweep found no public inherent
method names absent from compatibility docs. This scan is a name crosswalk;
it does not prove trait/inherited surfaces or Java overload/input/error/flow
parity.

Pinned Java source inspection confirmed `TopicValidator.getSystemTopicSet()`
and `getNotAllowedSendTopicSet()` are public; the underlying fields are
private. Existing Rust accessors map those public methods, so no code boundary
change was appropriate.

